{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01211",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 4.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Hi doctor, am I too early?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.64,
      "end_seconds": 11.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "yes, come in and sit down. What brings you here today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 12.05,
      "end_seconds": 23.66,
      "duration_seconds": 11.61,
      "text": "Erm, uh, it's yellow eyes. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 24.5,
      "end_seconds": 27.56,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.54,
      "end_seconds": 40.38,
      "duration_seconds": 10.84,
      "text": "Honestly I can't say exactly when it started. It might have been last month or the month before, I really can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 41.71,
      "end_seconds": 43.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "any other symptoms with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.05,
      "end_seconds": 54.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.65,
      "text": "A dull ache on the right side of the tummy goes along with it, you know, most of the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 55.82,
      "end_seconds": 59.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "what about dark urine, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.24,
      "end_seconds": 64.69,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, six months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 66.18,
      "end_seconds": 69.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Did you get weight loss or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.06,
      "end_seconds": 73.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "none of those, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.91,
      "end_seconds": 80.51,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "and what about swelling of the tummy, black stools or vomiting blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.02,
      "end_seconds": 87.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.15,
      "text": "Okay, so no, I haven't had any of them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.82,
      "end_seconds": 91.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Is your chest okay generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.1,
      "end_seconds": 94.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.79,
      "text": "No, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.64,
      "end_seconds": 103.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "anything with your heart, like skipped beats or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.23,
      "end_seconds": 106.78,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.6,
      "end_seconds": 119.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 121.0,
      "end_seconds": 123.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "No, not at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.81,
      "end_seconds": 134.43,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Tell me about your routine, work, habits, that sort of thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.01,
      "end_seconds": 144.87,
      "duration_seconds": 9.86,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days. I swim twice a week. My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.72,
      "end_seconds": 162.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.04,
      "end_seconds": 165.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "I have diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.36,
      "end_seconds": 167.26,
      "duration_seconds": 0.9,
      "text": "right, right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 171.73,
      "end_seconds": 173.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.75,
      "text": "Yes, high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.22,
      "end_seconds": 184.34,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "Right, so high cholesterol is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.26,
      "end_seconds": 204.37,
      "duration_seconds": 18.11,
      "text": "It's Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day for my sugar. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible. Rosuvastatin. I take it 10 milligrams, at night. Glibenclamide I don't take anymore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.41,
      "end_seconds": 211.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.14,
      "text": "any allergies to tablets, food or anything in the the environment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.23,
      "end_seconds": 217.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.27,
      "text": "yes, nickel. I get a rash on my skin"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.27,
      "end_seconds": 227.83,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Let me take your readings now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.45,
      "end_seconds": 243.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.23,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.07,
      "end_seconds": 268.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "okay: pulse 78, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature 36.8, blood pressure 114 over 68."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 270.25,
      "end_seconds": 271.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.59,
      "end_seconds": 275.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.53,
      "text": "That's fine, I'll explain it soon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.79,
      "end_seconds": 281.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.03,
      "end_seconds": 283.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.18,
      "text": "Okay, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.09,
      "end_seconds": 286.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.14,
      "end_seconds": 304.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Liver edge is just palpable and mildly tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 309.45,
      "end_seconds": 327.68,
      "duration_seconds": 18.23,
      "text": "thank you, you can get dressed okay, so my impression is this: This looks most like jaundice with a cause we still need to find that's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 333.28,
      "end_seconds": 336.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Is there something to to worry about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 338.46,
      "end_seconds": 354.74,
      "duration_seconds": 16.28,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like jaundice with a cause we still need to find, but I'd like to confirm. I think an ultrasound of the abdomen makes sense here, for jaundice."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.46,
      "end_seconds": 357.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Does it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 359.1,
      "end_seconds": 366.64,
      "duration_seconds": 7.54,
      "text": "please avoid alcohol completely and don't take any painkillers except paracetamol, and not much of that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 367.07,
      "end_seconds": 375.74,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Ah. I'll want another look in three days. Right, is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 377.52,
      "end_seconds": 382.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Right, uh, I'll do that. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}